# Projects are numbered folders, and each lives in its own repository. They are
# cloned here side by side for local work, so they are ignored rather than
# absent -- this repo must not carry another project's data.
#
# The rule is by PATTERN so a new project does not have to be added by hand,
# and new ones do not sit in `git status` as untracked noise.
#
# THE EXCEPTION IS LOAD-BEARING. 04_Adventure_Works is this repository's own
# project -- it is tracked, and it is the reason the repo exists. Without the
# negation below, a blanket numbered-folder rule would ignore the very content
# this repo is for, and the next `git add -A` after a re-clone would quietly
# leave it out while everything still looked correct on disk.
[0-9][0-9]_*/
!04_Adventure_Works/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Presentation material that is not framework code. Untracking alone does not
# stick -- a blanket `git add -A` re-adds it, which is how it landed twice.
#
# Scoped to the FILE, never the directory: AzureFabricMCP/ now holds the whole
# framework, and ignoring it wholesale would drop the framework from the repo
# on the next commit while everything still looked fine on disk.
/AzureFabricMCP/Quiz_AI_Master_Orchestrator.md
